{"title":"2024 CMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10e5c2c9ab2bb89e782a30b00efd156e8c0bae7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> be an irrational number and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer such that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a51daa5cf5c99c66d15c4d8da98ed6918f6d89d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L &gt; \\frac{\\alpha^2}{\\alpha-1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"42\" />\nConsider a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> defined as follows: choose any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856a9e81f38296b38f366d672fe22751e69b6905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &gt; L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />, and for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fb60295e07513a936ba96c7a4455190de157b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} = \\begin{cases} \\lfloor \\alpha x_n \\rfloor, &amp; \\text{if } x_n \\le L, \\\\[6pt] \\lfloor x_n / \\alpha \\rfloor, &amp; \\text{if } x_n &gt; L. \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"233\" height=\"60\" />\n</p><p>Prove that (1) the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is eventually periodic, and (2) the eventual minimal period of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is an odd integer that does not depend on the choice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175305\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.004 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.005 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 31/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1941/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35545:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017175305 and revision id 277885. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}